main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ constant initializer: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ case label: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ default: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
expected constant expression
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
cbmc's constant evaluator (cpp_constexpr_eval.cpp, apply_side_effect)
gives up on an expression statement that is a function call, so
operator[] is not evaluated: "expected constant expression, but got
'(signed int)operator[](...)'" for the case label, a conversion error.
Without the `check(i);' statement the program verifies.
